   "appearance": "A small, quick young woman with ink on her fingertips and a red jasper seal on a cord round her wrist.",
   "backstory": "Tô Mộ Vân was born in 1176 at the old seat on the evening the glow filled the whole sky (C194). Her parents are the outer gate's steward Tô Bình Chu (to_binh_chu) and the dyer Hoàng Lan Chi (hoang_lan_chi). The head, her great-great-grand-aunt, came down from her hall that night, took her as a disciple before she had a name, and named her for the sky. At four she sorted the head's ledgers by the colour of their ink. At nine she was carried up to the Cloud Bridge with the sect (N-lac_ha-05). At fourteen she won the talisman contest at Hạc Đinh Thị against the scribes of Nam Phố Đường, who had held its prize seal for eleven contests (A203). She has three good roots and the head's patience for them. She is still at Luyện Khí at twenty-four because the head will not let her build a foundation until it can be perfect. Châu Phi Vân (chau_phi_van) has asked twice to borrow her for a season. Hình Lạc Nhạn (hinh_lac_nhan), twenty-six years older, is compared with her at every festival and loses every comparison.",
   "wants": "To build a perfect foundation on the Cloud Bridge at dusk, and to draw a talisman that keeps the evening glow after dark.",
   "secret": "Five years ago she followed the head into the locked gallery under the seat and read the first lines of the carving there by the head's lamp. The head did not see her. She has the lines by heart. She does not know they are the Deep Vein Scripture, the head's own secret art.",
